      "claim": "L3 oral-exposure records for the closely related azoles posaconazole (M01) and ketoconazole (M02) show measurable systemic exposure after oral dosing (e.g., posaconazole steady-state AUC 8619 ng·h/mL and Cmax 851 ng/mL; ketoconazole AUC0–24 53.9 µg·h/mL), supporting that the azole scaffold can be orally absorbed despite high MW and lipophilicity.",
