      "card_ids": ["C37","C38","C39","C40","C41","C42","C43","C44","C45","C46","C47","C48"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct itraconazole absolute-bioavailability record is present; all F values are from other molecules.",
    "The query condition is fasted, whereas several high-F records were obtained in fed or modified-release conditions; food/formulation effects may lower fasted F, though no fasted low-F evidence is supplied.",
    "L3 exposure records lack IV comparators, so they cannot quantify absolute oral bioavailability.",
    "The query's very high molecular weight (705), high logP/logD (~5.6), and lack of HBD are not fully represented by the smaller high-F comparators; transferability is uncertain.",
    "No low-F (<20%) context is available as a threshold-relevant negative control.",
    "L3 posaconazole Cmax values are variable across patient subgroups, but variability alone is not affirmative evidence for F < 20%."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted high (F ≥ 20%) because all visible L1 human absolute-bioavailability records are ≥49%, no affirmative low-F evidence exists, and L3 oral-exposure records for the closely related azoles posaconazole and ketoconazole show measurable oral absorption. The low physicochemical prior is not endpoint proof and is outweighed by the measured-F direction; confidence remains moderate because no direct fasted itraconazole F record is available."
}

